#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Ali was told to stay behind until he had returned the deposits people had left with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "‘Ali diminta untuk tetap tinggal hingga ia mengembalikan barang-barang yang dititipkan orang-orang kepada Nabi ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers came so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Para pencari mendekat sedemikian rupa hingga Abu Bakr berbisik, “Seandainya salah satu dari mereka melihat ke bawah ke arah kakinya, ia pasti melihat kita.” Nabi ﷺ menjawab, “Bagaimana dugaanmu tentang dua orang, sedangkan Allah menjadi yang ketiga?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Allah recalled this moment in the Quran: “the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us.’”"
msgstr "Allah mengenang saat ini dalam Al-Qur'an: “salah seorang dari dua orang ketika keduanya berada dalam gua, di waktu dia berkata kepada temannya: ‘Janganlah bersedih, sesungguhnya Allah bersama kita.’”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Ibn Ishaq’s telling, when the three nights had passed, Asma brought their food but had no strap to hang the bag. She undid her waist-belt and tied it on, and so she was called She of the Two Belts."
msgstr "Dalam penuturan Ibn Ishaq, setelah tiga malam berlalu, Asma membawakan makanan mereka tetapi tidak memiliki tali untuk menggantung kantongnya. Ia melepas ikat pinggangnya lalu mengikatkannya, dan karena itulah ia dijuluki Pemilik Dua Ikat Pinggang."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The pursuers climbed the mountain and passed the cave. Seeing a spider’s web across its opening, they said no one could have gone in there, and moved on. Ibn Kathir calls this report’s chain good."
msgstr "Para pengejar mendaki gunung dan melewati gua itu. Melihat sarang laba-laba menutupi mulut gua, mereka berkata tidak mungkin ada orang yang masuk ke sana, lalu beranjak pergi. Ibn Kathir menyebut sanad riwayat ini baik."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Some tell that the searchers saw a spider’s web across the cave’s opening, and walked on."
msgstr "Sebagian riwayat menyebutkan bahwa para pencari melihat sarang laba-laba di mulut gua, lalu berlalu begitu saja."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bukhari gives three nights. Which nights of the week they were comes from a later biography."
msgstr "Al-Bukhari menyebutkan tiga malam. Mengenai malam apa saja dalam sepekan itu, hal tersebut bersumber dari biografi setelahnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how the two reached a cave on Mount Thawr and hid there for three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan bagaimana keduanya sampai di sebuah gua di Gunung Thawr dan bersembunyi di sana selama tiga malam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how her brother ‘Abdullah spent the nights with them and brought them news from Makkah after dark."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan bagaimana saudaranya, ‘Abdullah, melewatkan malam bersama mereka dan membawakan kabar dari Makkah setelah hari gelap."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought the ewes to the cave each evening of the three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan bagaimana ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah membawa domba-domba perah ke gua setiap petang selama tiga malam itu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr recalls fearing that anyone who looked down at his own feet would see them."
msgstr "Abu Bakr mengingat rasa takutnya bahwa siapa pun yang melihat ke bawah kakinya sendiri akan melihat mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The verse speaks of the Prophet ﷺ as the second of two in the cave, telling his companion not to grieve."
msgstr "Ayat tersebut menceritakan Nabi ﷺ sebagai orang kedua dari dua orang di dalam gua, yang menenangkan sahabatnya agar tidak bersedih."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir explains the verse: Allah supported and aided His Messenger, who sheltered in the cave for three days."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir menjelaskan ayat tersebut: Allah mendukung dan menolong Rasul-Nya, yang berlindung di dalam gua selama tiga hari."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how Asma tied the food bag with her waist-belt, and so was called She of the Two Belts."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq menceritakan bagaimana Asma mengikat kantong makanan dengan ikat pinggangnya, sehingga dijuluki Pemilik Dua Ikat Pinggang."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The report of the spider’s web across the cave’s opening, whose chain Ibn Kathir calls good."
msgstr "Riwayat tentang sarang laba-laba di mulut gua, yang sanadnya dinilai baik oleh Ibn Kathir."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A modern biography names the three nights: the nights before Friday, Saturday and Sunday."
msgstr "Sebuah biografi modern menyebutkan ketiga malam tersebut: malam Jumat, Sabtu, dan Ahad."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "The number beside each book counts its source passages."
msgstr "Angka di samping setiap kitab menunjukkan jumlah kutipan sumbernya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr reached a cave on Mount Thawr and hid inside it. They would stay there for three nights."
msgstr "Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakr sampai di sebuah gua di Gunung Thawr dan bersembunyi di dalamnya. Mereka tinggal di sana selama tiga malam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each night, Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah slept near them. Before dawn he slipped back to Makkah, so that morning found him among Quraysh as if he had never left, and at dark he returned with any plot he had heard."
msgstr "Setiap malam, putra Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah, tidur di dekat mereka. Sebelum fajar, ia menyelinap kembali ke Makkah, sehingga saat pagi tiba ia sudah berada di tengah kaum Quraysh seakan-akan tidak pernah pergi, dan ketika hari gelap ia kembali membawa kabar tentang rencana apa pun yang ia dengar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah grazed a few milking ewes nearby and brought them to the cave after nightfall, so the two had milk. He did this on each of the three nights."
msgstr "Bekas budak Abu Bakr, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, menggembalakan beberapa ekor domba perah di dekat sana dan membawanya ke gua setelah malam tiba, sehingga keduanya memperoleh susu. Ia melakukan hal ini di setiap malam dari ketiga malam tersebut."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr slipped into a cave on Mount Thawr and stayed out of sight. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakr menyelinap ke sebuah gua di Gunung Thawr dan bersembunyi. Selama tiga malam, gua itu menjadi tempat persembunyian mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They were not alone for long. Each night Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah came after dark with whatever Quraysh were plotting, then slipped back before dawn, so that morning found him in Makkah as if he had never left."
msgstr "Mereka tidak lama sendirian. Setiap malam, putra Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah, datang setelah gelap untuk menyampaikan rencana apa pun yang sedang disusun Quraysh. Ia lalu menyelinap kembali sebelum fajar, sehingga pagi harinya ia sudah berada di Makkah seolah-olah tak pernah pergi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "And as darkness settled, Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought a few milking ewes to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. Every one of the three nights, he came."
msgstr "Saat malam tiba, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, bekas budak Abu Bakr yang telah dimerdekakan, membawa beberapa ekor domba betina ke gua untuk diperah, sehingga mereka berdua mendapat susu segar. Ia datang pada setiap malam selama tiga malam itu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the searchers came close, so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Kemudian para pencari itu mendekat, begitu dekat hingga Abu Bakr berbisik, “Jika salah seorang dari mereka melihat ke bawah, ke arah kakinya, ia akan melihat kita.” Nabi ﷺ menjawab, “Bagaimana menurutmu tentang dua orang yang Allah adalah yang ketiga bersama mereka?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Allah preserved that moment in the Quran: “the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us.’”"
msgstr "Allah mengabadikan peristiwa itu dalam Al-Qur’an: “yang kedua dari dua orang ketika keduanya berada di dalam gua, saat ia berkata kepada sahabatnya, ‘Jangan bersedih; Allah bersama kita.’”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Late that night the Prophet ﷺ left his house and set out with Abu Bakr, who carried all his savings with him. They did not take the road north to Madinah, but turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Larut malam itu, Nabi ﷺ meninggalkan rumahnya dan berangkat bersama Abu Bakr, yang membawa seluruh tabungannya. Mereka tidak mengambil jalan ke utara menuju Madinah, tetapi berbelok ke selatan, menuju Yaman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night, the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr quietly left Makkah. They went south, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Malam itu, Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakr diam-diam meninggalkan Makkah. Mereka bergerak ke selatan, berlawanan arah dari Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "About five miles on, they reached Mount Thawr. They climbed to a cave in its side and slipped inside, out of sight. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Sekitar lima mil kemudian, mereka tiba di Gunung Thawr. Mereka mendaki ke sebuah gua di lerengnya lalu masuk diam-diam, tak terlihat. Selama tiga malam, gua itu menjadi tempat persembunyian mereka."

