#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At al-‘Aqabah one pilgrimage season, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ recited the Quran to six men from Yathrib, who lived beside Jews. “By Allah,” they said to one another, “this is the prophet the Jews threatened you with.”"
msgstr "Pada suatu musim haji di al-‘Aqabah, Nabi Muhammad ﷺ membacakan Al-Qur’an kepada enam orang dari Yathrib, yang tinggal berdampingan dengan orang-orang Yahudi. “Demi Allah,” kata mereka satu sama lain, “inilah nabi yang diancamkan orang-orang Yahudi kepada kalian.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One pilgrimage season, six men from the town of Yathrib listened to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, and believed."
msgstr "Pada suatu musim haji, enam orang dari kota Yathrib mendengarkan Nabi Muhammad ﷺ, lalu beriman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each year more came, until seventy-three men and two women met him there by night and pledged to protect him as they protected their own women and children. “I am of you and you are of me,” he said."
msgstr "Setiap tahun, semakin banyak yang datang. Hingga akhirnya, tujuh puluh tiga pria dan dua perempuan menemuinya di sana pada malam hari dan berjanji akan melindunginya sebagaimana mereka melindungi perempuan dan anak-anak mereka sendiri. “Aku bagian dari kalian, dan kalian bagian dariku,” katanya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Later, many more came at night. They promised to keep him safe, just like their own families."
msgstr "Kemudian, semakin banyak orang datang pada malam hari. Mereka berjanji akan menjaganya seperti keluarga mereka sendiri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "“It is Yathrib,” he told his companions, and group after group they slipped away to Madinah. At last, of those free to go, only he, Abu Bakr and ‘Ali were left. And he waited for Allah’s permission to follow."
msgstr "“Yathrib,” katanya kepada para sahabatnya. Rombongan demi rombongan pun diam-diam berangkat ke Madinah. Akhirnya, di antara mereka yang bebas pergi, hanya beliau, Abu Bakr, dan ‘Ali yang tersisa. Beliau menunggu izin Allah untuk menyusul."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "So his friends moved to Yathrib, the town we call Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ waited for Allah’s permission to follow."
msgstr "Maka para sahabatnya pun pindah ke Yathrib, kota yang kita kenal sebagai Madinah. Nabi ﷺ menunggu izin Allah untuk menyusul."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr asked again and again to go. “Do not hurry,” he was told. “Perhaps Allah will give you a companion.” So he waited, hoping it would be the Prophet ﷺ, and fed two camels for four months to have them ready."
msgstr "Abu Bakr berkali-kali meminta izin untuk berangkat. “Jangan terburu-buru,” jawabnya. “Mungkin Allah akan memberimu seorang teman seperjalanan.” Maka Abu Bakr menunggu, berharap teman itu adalah Nabi ﷺ. Selama empat bulan, ia memberi makan dua ekor unta agar siap digunakan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr wanted to go too. He was told to wait: perhaps Allah would give him a companion."
msgstr "Abu Bakr juga ingin berangkat. Ia diminta menunggu: mungkin Allah akan memberinya seorang teman seperjalanan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then one day, in the full heat of noon, the Prophet ﷺ came at an hour he never came, and said, “Allah has given me permission to leave.” “Companionship?” Abu Bakr asked. “Companionship.” And Abu Bakr wept for joy."
msgstr "Suatu hari, saat tengah hari dan cuaca sangat panas, Nabi ﷺ datang pada waktu yang tidak biasa, lalu berkata, “Allah telah memberiku izin untuk berangkat.” “Bersama-sama?” tanya Abu Bakr. “Bersama-sama.” Abu Bakr pun menangis bahagia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One hot noon, the Prophet ﷺ came with the news: they could go together! Abu Bakr cried for joy."
msgstr "Pada suatu siang yang panas, Nabi ﷺ datang membawa kabar: mereka bisa berangkat bersama! Abu Bakr menangis bahagia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hired a guide to bring the camels to the cave of Thawr after three nights. Abu Bakr’s daughter Asma had nothing to tie up their food, so she split her waistband in two, and became “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Mereka menyewa seorang penunjuk jalan untuk membawa unta ke gua Thawr setelah tiga malam. Asma, putri Abu Bakr, tidak memiliki apa pun untuk mengikat bekal mereka. Ia pun membelah ikat pinggangnya menjadi dua, dan mendapat julukan “perempuan dengan dua ikat pinggang”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma had nothing to tie up their food, so she split her waistband in two and used that."
msgstr "Asma tidak punya apa pun untuk mengikat bekal mereka, jadi ia membelah ikat pinggangnya menjadi dua dan menggunakannya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, Quraysh had watched his companions go, and feared he would follow. In Dar al-Nadwah their leaders took Abu Jahl’s plan: young men from every clan would strike him together, spreading his blood across them all."
msgstr "Di Makkah, Quraysh menyaksikan para sahabatnya pergi dan khawatir beliau akan menyusul. Di Dar al-Nadwah, para pemimpin mereka menyetujui rencana Abu Jahl: para pemuda dari setiap kabilah akan menyerangnya bersama-sama, sehingga darahnya terbagi di antara mereka semua."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The leaders of Makkah were afraid of the Prophet ﷺ, and they made a plan to attack him."
msgstr "Para pemimpin Makkah takut kepada Nabi ﷺ, lalu menyusun rencana untuk menyerangnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night the men gathered at his door, waiting for him to sleep. He told ‘Ali to lie in his bed, wrapped in his green cloak. “Sleep in it,” he said. “Nothing you dislike will reach you from them.”"
msgstr "Malam itu, para lelaki berkumpul di depan pintunya, menunggu beliau tertidur. Beliau menyuruh ‘Ali berbaring di tempat tidurnya dengan berselimutkan jubah hijau. “Berbaringlah di situ,” katanya. “Tidak akan ada sesuatu yang buruk menimpamu dari mereka.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. ‘Ali lay in the Prophet’s bed, wrapped in his green cloak."
msgstr "Malam itu, mereka menunggu di luar pintunya. ‘Ali berbaring di tempat tidur Nabi dengan berselimutkan jubah hijau beliau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then he came out to them with a handful of dust, scattering it over their heads and reciting, “So We have covered them, and they do not see.” Allah took their sight from him, and he went on his way."
msgstr "Kemudian beliau keluar menghampiri mereka sambil membawa segenggam tanah. Beliau menaburkannya ke atas kepala mereka seraya membaca, “Lalu Kami menutupi mereka sehingga mereka tidak dapat melihat.” Allah menghalangi mereka melihat beliau, dan beliau pun melanjutkan perjalanan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ walked right out past them, scattering dust, and Allah kept them from seeing him."
msgstr "Nabi ﷺ berjalan melewati mereka sambil menaburkan tanah, dan Allah membuat mereka tidak dapat melihat beliau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came to Abu Bakr, and the two slipped out by a small door at the back of the house, Abu Bakr carrying all his savings. They did not take the road north to Madinah, but turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Beliau menemui Abu Bakr, lalu mereka berdua diam-diam keluar melalui pintu kecil di bagian belakang rumah. Abu Bakr membawa seluruh tabungannya. Mereka tidak mengambil jalan ke utara menuju Madinah, tetapi berbelok ke selatan, ke arah Yaman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He and his best friend, Abu Bakr, slipped away in the dark. They went south, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Beliau dan sahabat karibnya, Abu Bakr, diam-diam pergi dalam kegelapan. Mereka menuju selatan, berlawanan arah dari Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "About five miles on, they reached Mount Thawr and a cave in its side. Abu Bakr went in first, feeling his way in the dark, ready to take any harm himself. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Setelah menempuh sekitar lima mil, mereka tiba di Gunung Thawr dan sebuah gua di lerengnya. Abu Bakr masuk lebih dahulu, meraba-raba dalam gelap dan siap menanggung bahaya apa pun. Selama tiga malam, gua itu akan menjadi tempat persembunyian mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They reached a cave on Mount Thawr. Abu Bakr went in first to make sure it was safe."
msgstr "Mereka tiba di sebuah gua di Gunung Thawr. Abu Bakr masuk lebih dahulu untuk memastikan tempat itu aman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As darkness settled, Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought his milking sheep to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. At dawn he drove the flock along ‘Abdullah’s trail, and the sheep wiped out his footprints."
msgstr "Saat malam tiba, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, mantan budak Abu Bakr yang telah dimerdekakan, membawa kambing-kambing perahnya ke gua agar mereka berdua mendapat susu segar. Saat fajar, ia menggiring kawanan itu mengikuti jejak ‘Abdullah. Kaki-kaki kambing pun menghapus jejak langkahnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Amir brought sheep every evening for milk. In the morning, the sheep walked over ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "Setiap petang, ‘Amir membawa kambing untuk diambil susunya. Pada pagi hari, kambing-kambing itu berjalan melewati jejak kaki ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Searchers stood right above the cave! Abu Bakr was afraid they would look down. The Prophet ﷺ calmed his friend."
msgstr "Para pencari berdiri tepat di atas gua! Abu Bakr khawatir mereka akan melihat ke bawah. Nabi ﷺ menenangkan sahabatnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the guide came with the camels, as arranged, and now there were four of them, with ‘Amir riding behind Abu Bakr. The guide led them down below Makkah and out along the coast, “by the edge of the sea.”"
msgstr "Kemudian pemandu datang membawa unta-unta, sesuai kesepakatan. Kini ada empat unta, dengan ‘Amir menunggang di belakang Abu Bakr. Pemandu membawa mereka turun melewati bagian bawah Makkah, lalu menyusuri pesisir, “di tepi laut.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After three nights, their guide came with the camels, and they rode out along the coast by the sea."
msgstr "Setelah tiga malam, pemandu mereka datang membawa unta-unta, lalu mereka berkendara menyusuri pesisir di tepi laut."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People on the road knew Abu Bakr, but not the man with him. “Who is this man in front of you?” they asked. “This man guides me on the way,” he answered. They thought he meant the road; he meant the way of good."
msgstr "Orang-orang di jalan mengenal Abu Bakr, tetapi tidak mengenal orang yang bersamanya. “Siapa orang di hadapanmu ini?” tanya mereka. “Dia membimbingku di jalan,” jawabnya. Mereka mengira yang dimaksud adalah jalan yang dilalui; padahal yang dimaksud Abu Bakr adalah jalan kebaikan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People asked Abu Bakr who was with him. “He guides me on the way,” he said: the way of good."
msgstr "Orang-orang bertanya kepada Abu Bakr siapa yang bersamanya. “Dia membimbingku di jalan,” jawabnya—jalan kebaikan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh had put a price on the two. A man told Suraqah ibn Malik he had seen dark figures by the coast. “I knew that it was them,” Suraqah said, but he told the man otherwise. He wanted the hundred camels for himself."
msgstr "Quraysh menawarkan hadiah bagi siapa pun yang menangkap keduanya. Seorang lelaki memberi tahu Suraqah ibn Malik bahwa ia melihat sosok-sosok gelap di pesisir. “Aku tahu itu mereka,” kata Suraqah, tetapi ia mengatakan hal lain kepada lelaki itu. Ia ingin mendapatkan seratus unta itu untuk dirinya sendiri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the road by the sea, a rider called Suraqah raced after them on his horse, hoping for a big reward."
msgstr "Di jalan tepi laut, seorang penunggang bernama Suraqah mengejar mereka dengan kudanya, berharap mendapat hadiah besar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode hard until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ did not look back; Abu Bakr kept looking back. Then his horse’s forelegs sank into the ground up to the knees, and Suraqah fell."
msgstr "Ia memacu kudanya hingga dapat mendengar Nabi ﷺ membaca ayat-ayat. Nabi ﷺ tidak menoleh, sementara Abu Bakr terus menoleh ke belakang. Lalu kaki depan kudanya terperosok ke tanah hingga sebatas lutut, dan Suraqah pun terjatuh."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah called out for safety and offered them provisions. They asked only, “Keep our whereabouts hidden.” ‘Amir wrote him a letter of safety on leather, and Suraqah rode back, turning every pursuer home."
msgstr "Suraqah meminta jaminan keselamatan dan menawarkan bekal kepada mereka. Mereka hanya meminta, “Rahasiakan keberadaan kami.” ‘Amir menuliskan surat jaminan keselamatan untuknya di atas kulit, lalu Suraqah berkuda kembali dan menyuruh setiap pengejar pulang."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah gave up the chase. They asked him only to keep their secret, and he sent the other riders home."
msgstr "Suraqah menghentikan pengejarannya. Mereka hanya memintanya merahasiakan keberadaan mereka, lalu ia menyuruh para penunggang lain pulang."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They rode on, but their food had run out in a year of drought. By the road stood the two tents of Umm Ma‘bad, a woman who gave water and food to those who passed. They asked to buy meat and dates, but she had none."
msgstr "Mereka melanjutkan perjalanan, tetapi bekal makanan mereka telah habis di tengah tahun paceklik. Di tepi jalan berdiri dua tenda milik Umm Ma‘bad, seorang perempuan yang memberi air dan makanan kepada para musafir. Mereka ingin membeli daging dan kurma, tetapi ia tidak memilikinya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hungry and far from home, they stopped at the tent of Umm Ma‘bad. She had no food to give them."
msgstr "Dalam keadaan lapar dan jauh dari rumah, mereka berhenti di tenda Umm Ma‘bad. Ia tidak punya makanan untuk diberikan kepada mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the back of her tent stood a ewe too weak to follow the flock. The Prophet ﷺ passed his hand over her udder, spoke the name of Allah, and milked until froth rose over the vessel. Umm Ma‘bad drank first, he drank last."
msgstr "Di belakang tendanya ada seekor domba betina yang terlalu lemah untuk mengikuti kawanan. Nabi ﷺ mengusap ambingnya, menyebut nama Allah, lalu memerahnya hingga busa meluap dari wadah. Umm Ma‘bad minum lebih dahulu, dan beliau minum paling akhir."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Her thin sheep had no milk. The Prophet ﷺ said Allah’s name and milked her, and everyone drank!"
msgstr "Dombanya yang kurus tidak mengeluarkan susu. Nabi ﷺ menyebut nama Allah lalu memerahnya, dan semua orang pun minum!"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When her husband came home, she described their guest: a man of shining beauty, his words like beads slipping from a string. “By Allah,” said Abu Ma‘bad, “that is the man from Quraysh.”"
msgstr "Ketika suaminya pulang, ia menggambarkan tamu mereka: seorang lelaki yang rupawan, dengan kata-kata seperti manik-manik yang terurai dari seutas tali. “Demi Allah,” kata Abu Ma‘bad, “dialah lelaki dari Quraysh itu.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When her husband came home, she told him about their guest: a shining face, and words like beads on a string."
msgstr "Ketika suaminya pulang, ia bercerita tentang tamu mereka: wajah yang bercahaya dan kata-kata seperti manik-manik pada seutas tali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each morning the Muslims of Madinah watched for him till the heat drove them in. Then a man on a fort saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is your good fortune, the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Setiap pagi, kaum Muslim di Madinah menantikan kedatangannya hingga panas matahari membuat mereka masuk kembali. Lalu seorang lelaki di atas benteng melihat para musafir berpakaian putih berkilauan di tengah fatamorgana. “Inilah keberuntungan kalian, orang yang selama ini kalian nantikan!” serunya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Madinah, people waited every morning in the hot sun. At last a man shouted: he is here!"
msgstr "Di Madinah, orang-orang menunggu setiap pagi di bawah terik matahari. Akhirnya, seorang lelaki berseru, “Dia sudah tiba!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him at Quba, in the shade of a palm with Abu Bakr. Most had never seen him, and they greeted Abu Bakr. Then the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr held his cloak over him, and at that they knew him."
msgstr "Mereka menemukan beliau di Quba, berteduh di bawah pohon kurma bersama Abu Bakr. Kebanyakan dari mereka belum pernah melihat beliau, jadi mereka menyambut Abu Bakr. Lalu sinar matahari mengenai Nabi ﷺ. Abu Bakr menaungkan jubahnya kepada beliau, dan saat itulah mereka mengenali beliau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him resting in the shade of a palm tree at Quba, with Abu Bakr beside him."
msgstr "Mereka menemukan beliau sedang beristirahat di bawah naungan pohon kurma di Quba, dengan Abu Bakr di sisinya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There ‘Ali caught up with him, after three days in Makkah returning what people had left in the Prophet’s ﷺ care. The Prophet ﷺ founded his mosque at Quba and prayed in it, and on a Friday he rode on towards Madinah."
msgstr "Di sana, ‘Ali menyusul beliau setelah tiga hari di Makkah mengembalikan barang-barang yang dititipkan orang kepada Nabi ﷺ. Nabi ﷺ mendirikan masjid di Quba dan salat di sana. Pada hari Jumat, beliau berkendara melanjutkan perjalanan menuju Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At Quba he built a mosque and prayed in it. Then he rode on into Madinah."
msgstr "Di Quba, beliau membangun masjid dan salat di sana. Kemudian beliau berkendara melanjutkan perjalanan ke Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the way he prayed his first Friday prayer in Madinah. Clan after clan came out: “Stay with us. We have the numbers and the strength.” Each time he said of his camel, “Let her go her way; she is under orders.”"
msgstr "Dalam perjalanan, beliau menunaikan salat Jumat pertamanya di Madinah. Kabilah demi kabilah keluar menyambutnya. “Tinggallah bersama kami. Kami punya banyak orang dan kekuatan.” Setiap kali, beliau berkata tentang untanya, “Biarkan dia berjalan; dia sedang mendapat perintah.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last the Prophet ﷺ rode into Madinah. Family after family asked him to stay, but he let his camel walk on."
msgstr "Akhirnya Nabi ﷺ memasuki Madinah dengan berkendara. Keluarga demi keluarga memintanya untuk tinggal, tetapi beliau membiarkan untanya terus berjalan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The whole town poured out, and women on the rooftops strained to see: “Which one is he?” At last the camel knelt in a yard where dates were laid to dry. “This, if Allah wills, is the stopping place,” he said."
msgstr "Seluruh penduduk kota berbondong-bondong keluar, sementara para perempuan di atap berusaha melihat. “Yang mana orangnya?” Akhirnya, unta itu berlutut di halaman tempat kurma dijemur. “Inilah tempat persinggahan, jika Allah menghendaki,” kata beliau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Children ran and people climbed up high to see him. His camel knelt in a yard where dates were dried."
msgstr "Anak-anak berlarian dan orang-orang naik ke tempat yang tinggi untuk melihat beliau. Unta beliau berlutut di halaman tempat kurma dijemur."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There his mosque rose, from bricks of sun-dried clay. The Prophet ﷺ carried them with the others, chanting, “O Allah, there is no good but the good of the Hereafter, so help the Ansar and the Emigrants.”"
msgstr "Di sana masjidnya berdiri, dibangun dari bata tanah liat yang dijemur hingga kering. Nabi ﷺ mengangkat bata bersama yang lain sambil bersenandung, “Ya Allah, tiada kebaikan selain kebaikan akhirat, maka bantulah kaum Ansar dan kaum Muhajirin.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There they built a mosque, and the Prophet ﷺ carried bricks to help."
msgstr "Di sana mereka membangun masjid, dan Nabi ﷺ ikut mengangkat bata."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the fever of Madinah laid his companions low. Makkah had been the dearest of lands to him, and now he prayed for their new home: “O Allah, make Madinah dear to us as You made Makkah dear to us, or dearer.”"
msgstr "Kemudian demam Madinah membuat para sahabatnya jatuh sakit. Makkah adalah negeri yang paling dicintainya, dan kini ia berdoa untuk tempat tinggal baru mereka: “Ya Allah, jadikan Madinah kami cintai sebagaimana Engkau menjadikan Makkah kami cintai, atau lebih.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He prayed that Allah would make Madinah as dear to them as Makkah, and even dearer."
msgstr "Ia berdoa agar Allah menjadikan Madinah sama tercintanya bagi mereka seperti Makkah, bahkan lebih."

