#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bayhaqi, Dala'il al-Nubuwwah, 2/518"
msgstr "Al-Baihaqi, Dala'il al-Nubuwwah, 2/518"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers came close, so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Para pencari itu datang mendekat, begitu dekat hingga Abu Bakr berbisik, “Jika salah seorang dari mereka melihat ke bawah, ke arah kakinya, ia akan melihat kita.” Nabi ﷺ menjawab, “Bagaimana menurutmu tentang dua orang yang Allah menjadi yang ketiga bersama mereka?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Nor were they alone. Each night Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah came after dark with whatever Quraysh were plotting, then slipped back before dawn, so that morning found him in Makkah as if he had never left."
msgstr "Mereka juga tidak sendirian. Setiap malam, putra Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah, datang setelah gelap membawa kabar tentang rencana Quraysh, lalu menyelinap kembali sebelum fajar, sehingga pagi hari mendapati dirinya sudah berada di Makkah seolah-olah ia tidak pernah pergi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A home had to be offered before anyone could leave: the pledges at al-‘Aqabah gave the believers somewhere to go."
msgstr "Sebelum siapa pun bisa pergi, harus ada rumah yang bersedia menerima mereka. Janji setia di al-‘Aqabah memberi orang-orang beriman tempat untuk dituju."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Waiting on Allah’s permission and preparing every detail went together: camels fed for months, a guide hired, food packed."
msgstr "Menunggu izin Allah berjalan seiring dengan menyiapkan segala sesuatunya: unta diberi makan selama berbulan-bulan, seorang penunjuk jalan disewa, dan makanan dibawa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "His honesty held even then: on the night Quraysh plotted his death, he left ‘Ali to return all that Makkah had entrusted to him."
msgstr "Beliau tetap jujur bahkan saat itu: pada malam ketika Quraysh merencanakan pembunuhannya, beliau meminta ‘Ali mengembalikan semua barang yang dititipkan warga Makkah kepadanya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the most frightening moment came the calmest words: “Do not grieve; Allah is with us.”"
msgstr "Pada saat paling menakutkan, terucap kata-kata yang paling menenangkan: “Jangan bersedih, Allah bersama kita.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hunted as they were, they kept to the truth: “This man guides me on the way,” Abu Bakr said, and meant the way of good."
msgstr "Meski sedang diburu, mereka tetap berkata jujur. “Orang ini menunjukkan jalan kepadaku,” kata Abu Bakr, yang maksudnya jalan kebaikan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hearts can turn in a moment: the man who rode out to capture them rode back to send every pursuer home."
msgstr "Hati bisa berubah dalam sekejap: orang yang berangkat untuk menangkap mereka pulang untuk menyuruh semua pengejar kembali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Blessing came to a tent with nothing to give, and the Prophet ﷺ, who brought it, drank last of all."
msgstr "Keberkahan datang ke sebuah tenda yang tak punya apa-apa untuk diberikan. Nabi ﷺ, yang membawa keberkahan itu, minum paling akhir."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At Quba the Prophet ﷺ founded the first mosque where he prayed openly with his companions, a mosque built on God-consciousness."
msgstr "Di Quba, Nabi ﷺ mendirikan masjid pertama tempat beliau salat secara terbuka bersama para sahabatnya—masjid yang dibangun atas dasar takwa."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah became home by being built together: emigrants and Ansar raised the mosque side by side, and were made brothers."
msgstr "Madinah menjadi rumah karena dibangun bersama: kaum Muhajirin dan Ansar mendirikan masjid berdampingan dan dipersaudarakan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "You followed the Hijrah from a promise made by night at al-‘Aqabah to a prayer for Madinah: a long wait, three nights in a cave, a hunter turned protector, and a whole town out to welcome him."
msgstr "Kamu mengikuti kisah Hijrah, dari janji yang diucapkan pada malam hari di al-‘Aqabah hingga doa untuk Madinah: penantian panjang, tiga malam di dalam gua, seorang pemburu yang berubah menjadi pelindung, dan seluruh kota yang keluar untuk menyambut beliau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "His home, where he waited for permission and from where he slipped out by night with Abu Bakr."
msgstr "Rumah beliau, tempat beliau menunggu izin dan menyelinap pergi pada malam hari bersama Abu Bakr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr hid in a cave for three nights while Quraysh searched for them."
msgstr "Tempat Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakr bersembunyi di dalam gua selama tiga malam sementara Quraysh mencari mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide led them down to the sea and along the shore, station after station, towards Madinah."
msgstr "Penunjuk jalan membawa mereka turun ke laut lalu menyusuri pantai, dari satu tempat ke tempat berikutnya, menuju Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where Madinah’s Muslims first met him, under a palm, and where he founded his mosque."
msgstr "Tempat kaum Muslim Madinah pertama kali bertemu beliau, di bawah pohon kurma, dan tempat beliau mendirikan masjidnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Where his camel knelt, his mosque rose, and the emigrants made a new home."
msgstr "Tempat untanya berlutut, masjid beliau dibangun, dan kaum Muhajirin memulai kehidupan baru."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Under Abu Ayyub’s roof"
msgstr "Di bawah atap Abu Ayyub"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Ayyub carried the Prophet’s ﷺ saddle into his house. One day a jar of water broke upstairs, and he and his wife soaked it up with their only blanket, so that not a drop would fall on their guest."
msgstr "Abu Ayyub membawa pelana Nabi ﷺ ke dalam rumahnya. Suatu hari, sebuah wadah air pecah di lantai atas. Ia dan istrinya menyerap air itu dengan satu-satunya selimut mereka agar tak setetes pun menimpa tamu mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When water spilled upstairs, Abu Ayyub and his wife mopped it up with their only blanket, so none dripped on him."
msgstr "Saat air tumpah di lantai atas, Abu Ayyub dan istrinya menyerapnya dengan satu-satunya selimut mereka agar tak ada air yang menetes ke beliau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "She of the two waistbands"
msgstr "Perempuan dengan dua ikat pinggang"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In another telling, it was at the cave that Asma’s waistband served them. She had brought their food but forgotten a strap to hang it by, so she split her waistband in two and hung the bag with one half."
msgstr "Dalam kisah lain, ikat pinggang Asma membantu mereka di gua. Ia membawa makanan mereka, tetapi lupa membawa tali untuk menggantungnya. Maka ia membelah ikat pinggangnya menjadi dua dan menggantung kantong itu dengan salah satu bagiannya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma had nothing to tie up their food bag, so she split her waistband in two and used one half."
msgstr "Asma tidak punya apa pun untuk mengikat kantong makanan mereka. Maka ia membelah ikat pinggangnya menjadi dua dan memakai salah satu bagiannya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ made each emigrant a brother to one of the Ansar who had taken them in. Each pair stood by the other and shared what they had, and at first such brothers even inherited from one another."
msgstr "Nabi ﷺ mempersaudarakan setiap orang yang berhijrah dengan salah seorang Ansar yang menerima mereka. Setiap pasangan saling mendukung dan berbagi apa yang mereka miliki. Pada awalnya, saudara-saudara angkat ini bahkan saling mewarisi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He made each newcomer a brother to someone from Madinah, so they would help each other and share."
msgstr "Beliau mempersaudarakan setiap pendatang dengan seseorang dari Madinah agar mereka saling membantu dan berbagi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Let her go her way"
msgstr "Biarkan ia melanjutkan perjalanannya"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Even his mother’s kin, Banu ‘Adi ibn al-Najjar, called out, “Come to your mother’s people.” “Let her go her way,” he said. “She is under orders.” She walked on, and knelt among Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Bahkan kerabat dari pihak ibunya, Banu ‘Adi ibn al-Najjar, berseru, “Mari bergabung dengan kaum ibumu.” “Biarkan ia melanjutkan perjalanannya,” kata beliau. “Ia menjalankan tugas.” Perempuan itu pun melanjutkan perjalanan dan berlutut di tengah Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Everyone wanted the Prophet ﷺ to stay with them. “Let my camel go,” he said. “She knows where to stop.”"
msgstr "Semua orang ingin agar Nabi ﷺ tinggal bersama mereka. “Biarkan untaku berjalan,” katanya. “Ia tahu di mana harus berhenti.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode out of Quba on a Friday. On the way, the time for prayer came among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, and he prayed it in their mosque in the valley of Ranuna: his first Friday prayer in Madinah."
msgstr "Pada hari Jumat, beliau berangkat dengan menunggang unta dari Quba. Dalam perjalanan, waktu salat tiba saat beliau berada di tengah Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf. Beliau menunaikannya di masjid mereka di lembah Ranuna: salat Jumat pertamanya di Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On his way into Madinah, the Prophet ﷺ stopped to lead the Friday prayer for the very first time there."
msgstr "Dalam perjalanan menuju Madinah, Nabi ﷺ berhenti untuk mengimami salat Jumat untuk pertama kalinya di sana."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Dressed in white"
msgstr "Berpakaian putih"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the road they met al-Zubayr, coming home from Syria with Muslim merchants, and he dressed the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr in white. It was in white, shimmering in the mirage, that they were first seen from Madinah."
msgstr "Di perjalanan, mereka bertemu al-Zubayr yang sedang pulang dari Syam bersama para pedagang Muslim. Ia memberi Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakr pakaian putih. Dengan pakaian putih yang berkilau dalam fatamorgana, mereka terlihat dari Madinah untuk pertama kalinya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the way, their friend al-Zubayr gave them white clothes to wear."
msgstr "Dalam perjalanan, sahabat mereka, al-Zubayr, memberi mereka pakaian putih."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As he came, the women and children of Madinah sang: “The full moon has risen over us, from the passes of al-Wada‘. Thanks are due from us, as long as anyone calls to Allah.”"
msgstr "Saat beliau tiba, para perempuan dan anak-anak Madinah bernyanyi: “Bulan purnama telah terbit di atas kami, dari celah-celah al-Wada‘. Syukur wajib kami panjatkan selama masih ada yang menyeru kepada Allah.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The women and children sang a song of welcome: “The full moon has risen over us!”"
msgstr "Para perempuan dan anak-anak menyanyikan lagu sambutan: “Bulan purnama telah terbit di atas kami!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "South, not north"
msgstr "Ke selatan, bukan ke utara"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah lay to the north, but that was not the road they took. Under cover of night they turned the opposite way, south on the road towards Yemen, and went about five miles to Mount Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah terletak di utara, tetapi bukan itu arah yang mereka ambil. Dalam lindungan malam, mereka berbelok ke arah sebaliknya, ke selatan melalui jalan menuju Yaman, lalu menempuh sekitar lima mil ke Gunung Thawr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Madinah was to the north, but they went south first, to a mountain called Thawr."
msgstr "Madinah berada di utara, tetapi mereka lebih dulu pergi ke selatan, menuju gunung bernama Thawr."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The road by the sea"
msgstr "Jalan di tepi laut"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide led them down below Makkah and along the coast, out onto the road below ‘Usfan. Then he took them by lower Amaj, and back to the road past Qudayd, one station after another."
msgstr "Pemandu itu membawa mereka ke selatan Makkah menyusuri pesisir, lalu ke jalan di sebelah selatan ‘Usfan. Setelah itu, ia membawa mereka melewati bagian bawah Amaj dan kembali ke jalan yang melintasi Qudayd, dari satu tempat perhentian ke tempat berikutnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their guide knew the desert well. He led them down to the sea and along the coast, from one place to the next."
msgstr "Pemandu mereka mengenal gurun dengan baik. Ia membawa mereka ke arah laut dan menyusuri pesisir, dari satu tempat ke tempat berikutnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In the full heat of noon, someone called to Abu Bakr: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at the door, his head covered, at an hour he never came. “Allah has given me permission to leave,” he said."
msgstr "Saat tengah hari yang terik, seseorang memberi tahu Abu Bakr bahwa Rasulullah ﷺ berada di depan pintu dengan kepala tertutup—datang pada waktu yang tidak biasanya. “Allah telah mengizinkanku untuk berangkat,” katanya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One hot noon the Prophet ﷺ knocked at Abu Bakr’s door with big news: “Allah has given me permission to leave.”"
msgstr "Pada suatu siang yang panas, Nabi ﷺ mengetuk pintu Abu Bakr membawa kabar besar: “Allah telah mengizinkanku untuk berangkat.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "All his money"
msgstr "Seluruh hartanya"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When Abu Bakr slipped out with the Prophet ﷺ that night, by a small door at the back of his house, he carried all his money with him: five or six thousand dirhams."
msgstr "Malam itu, saat Abu Bakr diam-diam pergi bersama Nabi ﷺ melalui pintu kecil di belakang rumahnya, ia membawa seluruh hartanya: lima atau enam ribu dirham."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money with him for the journey, thousands of silver coins."
msgstr "Abu Bakr membawa seluruh hartanya dalam perjalanan itu, ribuan keping uang perak."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the mountain the trail grew confused, so the searchers climbed it and passed by the cave. Seeing a spider’s web across its entrance, they said, “If anyone had gone in here, there would be no web over it.”"
msgstr "Di gunung itu, jejak mereka sulit diikuti. Para pencari pun mendaki dan melewati gua. Ketika melihat jaring laba-laba menutupi pintu masuknya, mereka berkata, “Kalau ada yang masuk ke sini, pasti tidak akan ada jaring di sana.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers saw a spider’s web across the cave’s opening. “No one went in there,” they said, and walked on."
msgstr "Para pencari melihat jaring laba-laba menutupi mulut gua. “Tak ada yang masuk ke sana,” kata mereka, lalu melanjutkan perjalanan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah gives three nights. Which nights of the week they were was worked out by later biographers."
msgstr "‘Aishah menyebut tiga malam. Para penulis biografi yang datang kemudian memperkirakan malam-malam dalam pekan yang dimaksud."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Into Madinah, on a Friday"
msgstr "Memasuki Madinah pada hari Jumat"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Friday, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"
msgstr "Jumat, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq gives the Friday he left Quba; the day of the month was worked out by a modern biographer."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq menyebut bahwa beliau berangkat dari Quba pada hari Jumat; tanggal dalam bulan itu diperkirakan oleh seorang penulis biografi modern."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The guide comes with the camels"
msgstr "Pemandu datang bersama unta-unta"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Night of 1 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 16 September 622"
msgstr "Malam 1 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 16 September 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came after the third night, as agreed. Later biographers date it to the night of Monday."
msgstr "Ia datang setelah malam ketiga, sesuai kesepakatan. Para penulis biografi belakangan menyebut malam Senin sebagai waktunya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He had stayed on in Makkah through Muharram and Safar. The exact night was worked out by a modern biographer."
msgstr "Ia tetap tinggal di Makkah sepanjang Muharram dan Safar. Seorang penulis biografi modern memperkirakan malam yang tepat."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A Monday in Rabi‘ al-Awwal · September 622"
msgstr "Hari Senin di bulan Rabi‘ al-Awwal · September 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The reports agree it was a Monday. Ibn Ishaq gives the twelfth of the month; others give other days."
msgstr "Riwayat-riwayat sepakat bahwa hari itu adalah Senin. Ibn Ishaq menyebut tanggal dua belas bulan itu; riwayat lain menyebut tanggal yang berbeda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah on their trail"
msgstr "Suraqah membuntuti mereka"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A Tuesday, after the noon rest at Qudayd"
msgstr "Hari Selasa, setelah beristirahat siang di Qudayd"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Sa‘d gives this day; the other reports tell what happened in order, but name no day."
msgstr "Ibn Sa‘d menyebut hari ini; riwayat-riwayat lain menceritakan kejadian secara berurutan, tetapi tidak menyebut harinya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "From four days to fourteen nights"
msgstr "Dari empat hari hingga empat belas malam"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq counts Monday to Thursday; ‘Urwah speaks of ten nights and more, and Anas of fourteen."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq menghitung dari Senin hingga Kamis; ‘Urwah menyebut sepuluh malam lebih, sedangkan Anas menyebut empat belas malam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how many went ahead to Madinah, while Abu Bakr held himself back to travel with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan berapa orang yang berangkat lebih dahulu ke Madinah, sementara Abu Bakr menunda keberangkatannya agar bisa bepergian bersama Nabi ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah recalls the family making them ready in haste, and Asma tying the food bag with a piece of her waistband."
msgstr "‘Aishah mengenang keluarganya yang menyiapkan bekal mereka dengan tergesa-gesa, dan Asma mengikat kantong makanan dengan sepotong ikat pinggangnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how her brother ‘Abdullah spent the nights with them, was among Quraysh by morning, and brought their news after dark."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan bahwa saudaranya, ‘Abdullah, bermalam bersama mereka, lalu bergabung dengan Quraysh pada pagi hari dan membawa kabar kepada mereka setelah gelap."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought his milking sheep to the cave after nightfall, on each of the three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan bagaimana ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah membawa kambing perahnya ke gua setelah malam tiba, selama tiga malam berturut-turut."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how they hired a skilled guide of Banu al-Dil, gave him their two camels, and set the meeting at Thawr."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan bagaimana mereka menyewa seorang pemandu ulung dari Banu al-Dil, menyerahkan dua unta mereka kepadanya, dan menetapkan Thawr sebagai tempat pertemuan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah and the guide set out with them, and how the guide took them by the coast road."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan bagaimana ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah dan sang pemandu berangkat bersama mereka, dan bagaimana pemandu itu membawa mereka melalui jalan pesisir."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how Madinah heard he had left Makkah, and how he stayed among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf for ten nights and more."
msgstr "‘Urwah menceritakan bagaimana kabar bahwa ia telah meninggalkan Makkah sampai ke Madinah, dan bagaimana ia tinggal di tengah Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf selama sepuluh malam lebih."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how the yard was built into a mosque, with the Prophet ﷺ carrying bricks alongside the builders."
msgstr "‘Urwah menceritakan bagaimana halaman itu dibangun menjadi masjid, dengan Nabi ﷺ ikut mengangkat batu bata bersama para pekerja."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah recalls the blood-money offered for each of the two, and a man who had just seen dark figures by the coast."
msgstr "Suraqah mengenang hadiah uang tebusan yang ditawarkan untuk masing-masing dari keduanya, serta seorang laki-laki yang baru saja melihat sosok-sosok gelap di dekat pesisir."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah describes hearing the Prophet ﷺ recite, Abu Bakr looking back, and his own horse sinking to its knees."
msgstr "Suraqah menceritakan bagaimana ia mendengar Nabi ﷺ membaca ayat, Abu Bakr menoleh ke belakang, dan kudanya sendiri terperosok hingga lututnya menyentuh tanah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah recalls that they took nothing he offered and asked only for secrecy, and that ‘Amir wrote him a letter of safety on leather."
msgstr "Suraqah mengenang bahwa mereka tidak menerima apa pun yang ia tawarkan dan hanya meminta agar pertemuan itu dirahasiakan, lalu ‘Amir menuliskan surat perlindungan untuknya di atas kulit."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how he stayed among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf, founded the mosque built on God-consciousness, and prayed in it."
msgstr "‘Urwah menceritakan bagaimana ia tinggal di tengah Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf, mendirikan masjid yang dibangun atas dasar ketakwaan, dan beribadah di dalamnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells how people walked beside his camel until she knelt where his mosque now stands, then a yard for drying dates."
msgstr "‘Urwah menceritakan bagaimana orang-orang berjalan di sisi untanya hingga unta itu berlutut di tempat masjidnya kini berdiri, yang saat itu merupakan halaman untuk menjemur kurma."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how Quraysh, now afraid of him, met in Dar al-Nadwah, the house where they settled all their affairs."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq menceritakan bagaimana Quraysh, yang kini takut kepadanya, berkumpul di Dar al-Nadwah, rumah tempat mereka membahas dan memutuskan segala urusan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Seeing the men at his door, the Prophet ﷺ tells ‘Ali to sleep in his bed under his green cloak, and promises him safety."
msgstr "Melihat orang-orang di depan pintunya, Nabi ﷺ menyuruh ‘Ali tidur di ranjangnya dengan mengenakan jubah hijaunya, dan menjanjikan keselamatan kepadanya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells why ‘Ali stayed behind: anyone in Makkah who feared for something precious had left it with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq menjelaskan mengapa ‘Ali tinggal di belakang: siapa pun di Makkah yang khawatir akan barang berharga miliknya menitipkannya kepada Nabi ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Ibn Ishaq’s telling she has no food and only dry ewes; he milks one until the bowl froths: “Drink, Umm Ma‘bad.”"
msgstr "Dalam kisah Ibn Ishaq, perempuan itu tidak punya makanan dan hanya memiliki domba-domba betina yang kurus. Beliau memerah susu salah satunya hingga berbusa di mangkuk, lalu berkata, “Minumlah, Umm Ma‘bad.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah remembers the noon visit, and Abu Bakr asking at once to go with him: “Companionship?” “Yes.”"
msgstr "‘Aishah mengenang kunjungan pada tengah hari itu, dan Abu Bakr langsung meminta untuk pergi bersamanya: “Menemanimu?” “Ya.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma recalls her father taking all his money, and the stones she laid where it had been kept, under a cloth, to calm her grandfather."
msgstr "Asma mengenang ayahnya yang membawa semua uangnya, serta batu-batu yang ia letakkan di tempat penyimpanan uang itu, di bawah kain, untuk menenangkan kakeknya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri notes that he took the very opposite road from the one expected, south of Makkah towards Yemen."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri mencatat bahwa beliau mengambil jalan yang benar-benar berlawanan dari arah yang diperkirakan, menuju selatan dari Makkah ke arah Yaman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq places Asma’s waistband at the cave, and gives it as the reason she was called Dhat al-Nitaqayn."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq menuturkan bahwa Asma menggunakan ikat pinggangnya di gua, dan menyebutnya sebagai alasan ia dijuluki Dhat al-Nitaqayn."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn ‘Abbas tells of the web across the cave’s mouth; Ibn Kathir counts this among the best reports of it."
msgstr "Ibn ‘Abbas mengisahkan jaring laba-laba yang menutupi mulut gua; Ibn Kathir menilai kisah ini termasuk riwayat terbaik tentangnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq names the places on the guide’s route, one by one, from below Makkah to the road beyond Qudayd."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq menyebutkan tempat-tempat yang dilalui sang penunjuk jalan satu per satu, dari selatan Makkah hingga jalan di luar Qudayd."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah tells of the meeting with al-Zubayr’s caravan of Muslim merchants, and the white clothes he gave the two travellers."
msgstr "‘Urwah mengisahkan pertemuan dengan rombongan pedagang Muslim milik al-Zubayr, serta pakaian putih yang diberikannya kepada kedua musafir itu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri tells of the first Friday prayer among Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, with a hundred men, in the mosque in the valley."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri mengisahkan salat Jumat pertama di tengah Banu Salim ibn ‘Awf, yang diikuti seratus orang, di masjid di lembah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how each clan was answered, “Let her go, for she is under orders,” until she knelt among Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq mengisahkan bagaimana setiap kabilah dijawab, “Biarkan dia pergi, sebab dia menjalankan perintah,” hingga akhirnya unta itu berlutut di tengah Banu Malik ibn al-Najjar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how he lodged with Abu Ayyub until his mosque and rooms were built, working on them with emigrants and Ansar."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq mengisahkan bahwa beliau tinggal bersama Abu Ayyub hingga masjid dan kamar-kamarnya selesai dibangun; kaum Muhajirin dan Ansar turut mengerjakannya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir’s heading for the brotherhood: the Prophet ﷺ paired emigrants with Ansar so each newcomer had someone to lean on."
msgstr "Judul Ibn Kathir tentang persaudaraan: Nabi ﷺ mempersaudarakan kaum Muhajirin dengan kaum Ansar agar setiap pendatang memiliki seseorang yang dapat diandalkan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn ‘A'ishah, a later narrator who does not say who told him, describes women and children singing as the Prophet ﷺ arrived."
msgstr "Ibn ‘A'ishah, seorang perawi dari masa kemudian yang tidak menyebutkan siapa sumber ceritanya, menggambarkan para perempuan dan anak-anak bernyanyi saat Nabi ﷺ tiba."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates the night he left his house: 27 Safar, in the fourteenth year of his prophethood."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri menyebut tanggal malam beliau meninggalkan rumahnya: 27 Safar, pada tahun keempat belas kenabian."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri names the three nights in the cave: the nights before Friday, Saturday and Sunday."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri menyebut tiga malam yang dihabiskan di gua: malam sebelum Jumat, Sabtu, dan Minggu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates the guide’s coming with the two camels to the night of Monday, the first of Rabi‘ al-Awwal."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri menyebut bahwa sang penunjuk jalan datang membawa dua unta pada malam Senin, tanggal satu Rabi‘ al-Awwal."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Urwah gives the day he came down among Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf: a Monday in the month of Rabi‘ al-Awwal."
msgstr "‘Urwah menyebut hari beliau tiba di tengah Banu ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf: hari Senin pada bulan Rabi‘ al-Awwal."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir sets Ibn Ishaq’s four days, Monday to Thursday, beside ‘Urwah’s report of ten nights and more."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir membandingkan keterangan Ibn Ishaq tentang empat hari, dari Senin hingga Kamis, dengan riwayat ‘Urwah tentang sepuluh malam atau lebih."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Mubarakfuri dates his arrival among Banu al-Najjar to Friday, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal, in the first year of the Hijrah."
msgstr "Al-Mubarakfuri menyebut bahwa beliau tiba di tengah Banu al-Najjar pada Jumat, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal, tahun pertama Hijrah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir gives her name, ‘Atikah, and her family, and calls her story well known, through routes that support one another."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir menyebut namanya, ‘Atikah, serta keluarganya. Ia mengatakan kisahnya dikenal luas dan diriwayatkan melalui jalur-jalur yang saling menguatkan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Stones under a cloth"
msgstr "Batu-batu di bawah kain"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money, five or six thousand dirhams. When his blind father came, fearing it gone, Asma laid stones in its niche under a cloth and let him feel them."
msgstr "Abu Bakr membawa seluruh hartanya, lima atau enam ribu dirham. Ketika ayahnya yang buta datang dan khawatir hartanya sudah hilang, Asma meletakkan batu-batu di tempat penyimpanannya, menutupinya dengan kain, lalu membiarkan ayahnya merabanya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money. To calm her blind grandfather, Asma let him feel stones under a cloth."
msgstr "Abu Bakr membawa seluruh hartanya. Untuk menenangkan kakeknya yang buta, Asma membiarkannya meraba batu-batu di bawah kain."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Monday 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · September 622"
msgstr "Senin, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · September 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq’s date. The reports agree on a Monday but differ on the day of the month."
msgstr "Tanggal menurut Ibn Ishaq. Berbagai riwayat sepakat bahwa hari itu adalah Senin, tetapi berbeda mengenai tanggalnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Friday after Quba · Rabi‘ al-Awwal 622"
msgstr "Hari Jumat setelah Quba · Rabi‘ al-Awwal 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq has him stay at Quba from Monday to Thursday and ride on to Madinah on the Friday."
msgstr "Menurut Ibn Ishaq, beliau tinggal di Quba dari hari Senin hingga Kamis, lalu berkendara menuju Madinah pada hari Jumat."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "Verification failed. Try again."
msgstr "Verifikasi gagal. Coba lagi."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "Retry verification"
msgstr "Coba verifikasi lagi"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. ‘Ali lay in the Prophet’s ﷺ bed, wrapped in his green cloak."
msgstr "Malam itu, mereka menunggu di luar pintunya. ‘Ali berbaring di ranjang Nabi ﷺ, berselimutkan jubah hijau beliau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s helper ‘Amir brought sheep each evening for milk. At dawn the sheep walked over ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "‘Amir, pembantu Abu Bakr, membawa kambing setiap petang untuk diambil susunya. Saat fajar, kambing-kambing itu berjalan melewati jejak kaki ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Some say it was here that Abu Bakr’s daughter Asma split her waistband in two, to tie up their food bag."
msgstr "Ada yang mengatakan bahwa di sinilah Asma, putri Abu Bakr, membelah ikat pinggangnya menjadi dua untuk mengikat kantong bekal mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr took all his money. To calm her blind grandfather, his daughter Asma let him feel stones under a cloth."
msgstr "Abu Bakr membawa seluruh hartanya. Untuk menenangkan kakeknya yang tunanetra, putrinya, Asma, membiarkannya meraba batu-batu di balik kain."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Friday 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"
msgstr "Jumat, 12 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 27 September 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq has him stay at Quba Monday to Thursday and ride on the Friday; a modern biographer worked out the date."
msgstr "Menurut Ibn Ishaq, beliau tinggal di Quba dari Senin hingga Kamis, lalu berangkat dengan berkendara pada Jumat; seorang penulis biografi modern menghitung tanggalnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bukhari’s report has him come on the morning of the third day; later biographers date it to the night of Monday."
msgstr "Riwayat al-Bukhari menyebut beliau tiba pada pagi hari ketiga; para penulis biografi belakangan menetapkan waktunya pada malam Senin."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Monday 8 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 23 September 622"
msgstr "Senin, 8 Rabi‘ al-Awwal · 23 September 622"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The reports agree on a Monday. A modern biographer worked out the date; Ibn Ishaq gives the twelfth."
msgstr "Berbagai riwayat sepakat bahwa harinya adalah Senin. Seorang penulis biografi modern menghitung tanggalnya; Ibn Ishaq menyebut tanggal dua belas."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After the noon rest at Qudayd"
msgstr "Setelah beristirahat pada tengah hari di Qudayd"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Sa‘d calls it a Tuesday, by his own count of the days; the other reports name no day."
msgstr "Menurut hitungan hari versinya sendiri, Ibn Sa‘d menyebutnya hari Selasa; riwayat-riwayat lain tidak menyebutkan harinya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every pilgrimage season, as the tribes came to Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ went out to them and called them to Allah. One season, at a place called al-‘Aqabah, six men from Yathrib sat down to listen."
msgstr "Setiap musim haji, saat berbagai kabilah datang ke Makkah, Nabi ﷺ mendatangi mereka dan menyeru mereka kepada Allah. Pada suatu musim, di tempat bernama al-‘Aqabah, enam orang dari Yathrib duduk untuk mendengarkan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every year, pilgrims came to Makkah. The Prophet ﷺ told them about Allah, and six men from Yathrib listened."
msgstr "Setiap tahun, para jemaah haji datang ke Makkah. Nabi ﷺ bercerita kepada mereka tentang Allah, dan enam orang dari Yathrib mendengarkan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At home their Jewish neighbours often warned of a prophet soon to come. “By Allah,” the six said to one another, “this is the prophet they threatened us with.” They accepted Islam and took it home."
msgstr "Di kampung halaman mereka, para tetangga Yahudi sering memperingatkan bahwa seorang nabi akan segera datang. “Demi Allah,” kata keenam orang itu satu sama lain, “inilah nabi yang mereka ancamkan kepada kita.” Mereka memeluk Islam dan membawa ajaran itu pulang."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their Jewish neighbours said a prophet was coming. “This is him!” the six men said, and they became Muslims."
msgstr "Para tetangga Yahudi mereka berkata bahwa seorang nabi akan datang. “Inilah dia!” kata keenam orang itu, lalu mereka memeluk Islam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, those who followed the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ were insulted and harmed by Quraysh, his own tribe, who ruled the town. This is the story of the Hijrah: how they found a new home, and how he made the journey there."
msgstr "Di Makkah, orang-orang yang mengikuti Nabi Muhammad ﷺ dihina dan disakiti oleh Quraysh, sukunya sendiri yang menguasai kota itu. Inilah kisah Hijrah: bagaimana mereka menemukan rumah baru, dan bagaimana beliau melakukan perjalanan ke sana."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, the Prophet’s ﷺ own tribe was cruel to the Muslims. This is the story of how they found a new home."
msgstr "Di Makkah, suku Nabi ﷺ sendiri berlaku kejam terhadap kaum Muslim. Inilah kisah tentang bagaimana mereka menemukan rumah baru."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every pilgrimage season, as tribes from across Arabia came to Makkah, the Prophet ﷺ went out to them and called them to Allah. One season, at al-‘Aqabah, six men from Yathrib, a town to the north, sat down to listen."
msgstr "Setiap musim haji, saat berbagai suku dari seluruh penjuru Arabia datang ke Makkah, Nabi ﷺ menemui mereka dan menyeru mereka kepada Allah. Pada suatu musim, di al-‘Aqabah, enam pria dari Yathrib, sebuah kota di sebelah utara, duduk untuk mendengarkan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Every year, visitors came to Makkah to worship. The Prophet ﷺ told them about Allah, and six men from Yathrib listened."
msgstr "Setiap tahun, para pengunjung datang ke Makkah untuk beribadah. Nabi ﷺ bercerita kepada mereka tentang Allah, dan enam pria dari Yathrib mendengarkan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Back home, their Jewish neighbours used to say a prophet would soon come, and they would follow him against them. “By Allah,” the six said to one another, “this is that prophet.” They accepted Islam and took it home."
msgstr "Di kampung halaman, tetangga-tetangga Yahudi mereka biasa berkata bahwa seorang nabi akan segera datang, lalu mereka akan mengikutinya untuk melawan orang-orang Yathrib. “Demi Allah,” kata keenam pria itu satu sama lain, “inilah nabi yang dimaksud.” Mereka memeluk Islam dan membawa ajaran itu pulang."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Back home, their Jewish neighbours said a prophet was coming. “This is him!” the six said, and they became Muslims."
msgstr "Di kampung halaman, tetangga-tetangga Yahudi mereka berkata bahwa seorang nabi akan datang. “Inilah orangnya!” kata keenam pria itu, lalu mereka menjadi Muslim."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each year more came from Yathrib, until seventy-three men and two women met him there by night. They pledged to protect him, if he came, as they protected their own families. “I am of you and you are of me,” he said."
msgstr "Setiap tahun, semakin banyak orang dari Yathrib datang, hingga pada suatu malam tujuh puluh tiga pria dan dua perempuan bertemu dengannya di sana. Mereka berjanji akan melindunginya jika beliau datang, sebagaimana mereka melindungi keluarga sendiri. “Aku bagian dari kalian, dan kalian bagian dariku,” katanya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Later, many more came from Yathrib at night. They promised to keep him safe, the way they kept their own families safe."
msgstr "Kemudian, lebih banyak lagi orang dari Yathrib datang pada malam hari. Mereka berjanji akan menjaganya tetap aman, seperti mereka menjaga keluarga sendiri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Their new home, he told his companions, would be Yathrib, soon to be called Madinah. Group by group these Emigrants slipped away, until few were left but him, his close friend Abu Bakr and his cousin ‘Ali."
msgstr "Beliau memberi tahu para sahabatnya bahwa rumah baru mereka adalah Yathrib, yang kelak akan disebut Madinah. Kelompok demi kelompok kaum Muhajirin pergi diam-diam, hingga hanya sedikit yang tersisa: beliau, sahabat dekatnya Abu Bakr, dan sepupunya ‘Ali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "So the Muslims of Makkah moved to Yathrib, the town we call Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ waited for Allah’s permission to go."
msgstr "Maka kaum Muslim di Makkah pindah ke Yathrib, kota yang kita sebut Madinah. Nabi ﷺ menunggu izin Allah untuk berangkat."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr asked again and again to go too. “Do not hurry,” the Prophet ﷺ told him. “Perhaps Allah will give you a companion.” Abu Bakr hoped it would be the Prophet ﷺ himself, and fed two camels for four months."
msgstr "Abu Bakr berkali-kali meminta agar diizinkan ikut pergi. “Jangan terburu-buru,” kata Nabi ﷺ kepadanya. “Mungkin Allah akan memberimu seorang teman seperjalanan.” Abu Bakr berharap orang itu adalah Nabi ﷺ sendiri, lalu selama empat bulan ia memberi makan dua ekor unta."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then one noon, at an hour he never came, the Prophet ﷺ came to Abu Bakr’s house. “Allah has given me permission to leave.” “And I am to come with you?” Abu Bakr asked. “Yes.” And Abu Bakr wept for joy."
msgstr "Lalu pada suatu siang, pada waktu yang biasanya beliau tidak datang, Nabi ﷺ mendatangi rumah Abu Bakr. “Allah telah memberiku izin untuk berangkat.” “Dan aku ikut bersamamu?” tanya Abu Bakr. “Ya.” Abu Bakr pun menangis bahagia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hired a guide to bring the camels after three nights to a cave on Mount Thawr, where they would hide. Asma, Abu Bakr’s daughter, split her waistband to tie up their food, and became “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Mereka menyewa seorang penunjuk jalan untuk membawa unta-unta ke sebuah gua di Gunung Thawr setelah tiga malam, tempat mereka akan bersembunyi. Asma, putri Abu Bakr, membelah ikat pinggangnya untuk mengikat bekal mereka. Karena itu, ia dikenal sebagai “perempuan pemilik dua ikat pinggang”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh feared the Prophet ﷺ would follow his companions. In their council house, their leaders agreed to kill him: a young man from every clan would strike at once, so that no one clan could be made to answer for it."
msgstr "Quraysh khawatir Nabi ﷺ akan menyusul para sahabatnya. Di balai musyawarah mereka, para pemimpin sepakat untuk membunuh beliau: seorang pemuda dari setiap kabilah akan menyerang sekaligus, sehingga tak ada satu kabilah pun yang dapat dimintai pertanggungjawaban."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last Allah gave him permission. But the leaders of Makkah, afraid of his message, made a plan to hurt him."
msgstr "Akhirnya Allah memberinya izin. Namun, para pemimpin Makkah yang takut pada ajarannya menyusun rencana untuk mencelakainya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. His cousin ‘Ali lay in his bed, so they would think the Prophet ﷺ was inside."
msgstr "Malam itu, mereka menunggu di luar pintunya. Sepupunya, ‘Ali, berbaring di tempat tidurnya agar mereka mengira Nabi ﷺ berada di dalam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then he came out to them with a handful of dust, scattering it over their heads and reciting the Quran: “So We have covered them, and they do not see.” Allah took their sight from him, and he went on his way."
msgstr "Lalu beliau keluar menemui mereka sambil membawa segenggam debu, menaburkannya ke atas kepala mereka dan membaca Al-Qur’an: “Lalu Kami menutupi mereka sehingga mereka tidak dapat melihat.” Allah menghalangi mereka melihat beliau, dan beliau pun melanjutkan perjalanan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ walked right out past them, throwing a handful of dust, and Allah kept them from seeing him."
msgstr "Nabi ﷺ berjalan keluar melewati mereka sambil menaburkan segenggam debu, dan Allah membuat mereka tidak dapat melihat beliau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came to Abu Bakr, and the two slipped out by a small door at the back of Abu Bakr’s house, Abu Bakr carrying all his savings. Madinah lay to the north, but they turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Beliau menemui Abu Bakr, lalu mereka berdua menyelinap keluar lewat pintu kecil di belakang rumah Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr membawa seluruh tabungannya. Madinah berada di utara, tetapi mereka menuju ke selatan, ke arah Yaman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He and his best friend, Abu Bakr, slipped away in the dark. They went south first, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Beliau dan sahabat karibnya, Abu Bakr, pergi diam-diam dalam gelap. Mula-mula mereka menuju ke selatan, ke arah yang berlawanan dari Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hid in a cave on Mount Thawr. Abu Bakr went in first to make sure it was safe."
msgstr "Mereka bersembunyi di sebuah gua di Gunung Thawr. Abu Bakr masuk lebih dahulu untuk memastikan tempat itu aman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh sent out searchers, and they came so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” “What do you think of two,” said the Prophet ﷺ, “when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Quraysh mengirim orang-orang untuk mencari mereka. Para pencari itu datang begitu dekat hingga Abu Bakr berbisik, “Jika salah seorang dari mereka melihat ke arah kakinya, ia akan melihat kita.” “Bagaimana menurutmu tentang dua orang,” kata Nabi ﷺ, “yang Allah menjadi yang ketiga?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Men from Makkah searched everywhere, and stood right above the cave! Abu Bakr was afraid. The Prophet ﷺ calmed him."
msgstr "Orang-orang dari Makkah mencari ke mana-mana dan berdiri tepat di atas gua! Abu Bakr merasa takut. Nabi ﷺ menenangkannya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As darkness settled, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, who tended Abu Bakr’s sheep, brought the flock to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. At dawn he drove it along ‘Abdullah’s trail, and the sheep wiped out ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "Saat malam tiba, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, yang menggembalakan domba-domba Abu Bakr, membawa kawanan itu ke gua agar mereka berdua mendapat susu segar. Saat fajar, ia menggiringnya menyusuri jejak ‘Abdullah, dan domba-domba itu menghapus jejak kaki ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s helper ‘Amir brought sheep each evening for milk. At dawn the sheep covered up ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "Setiap petang, ‘Amir, pembantu Abu Bakr, membawa domba-domba agar mereka mendapat susu. Saat fajar, domba-domba itu menutupi jejak kaki ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh offered a hundred camels for the two. Suraqah ibn Malik, a horseman of a tribe on the coast road, heard that riders had been seen by the sea. He knew it was them, but kept quiet: he wanted the reward himself."
msgstr "Quraisy menawarkan seratus unta untuk menangkap mereka berdua. Suraqah ibn Malik, seorang penunggang kuda dari suku yang tinggal di jalur pesisir, mendengar kabar bahwa ada para penunggang yang terlihat di dekat laut. Ia tahu bahwa merekalah orangnya, tetapi ia diam saja: ia ingin mendapatkan hadiah itu sendiri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After three nights they rode on by the sea. A rider called Suraqah raced after them, hoping for a reward."
msgstr "Setelah tiga malam, mereka melanjutkan perjalanan dengan berkendara di dekat laut. Seorang penunggang kuda bernama Suraqah mengejar mereka dengan harapan mendapat hadiah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode hard until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ did not look back; Abu Bakr kept looking back. Then Suraqah’s horse sank into the ground up to its knees, and he fell."
msgstr "Ia memacu kudanya sekuat tenaga hingga dapat mendengar Nabi ﷺ membaca. Nabi ﷺ tidak menoleh, sedangkan Abu Bakr terus menoleh ke belakang. Lalu kaki kuda Suraqah terperosok ke dalam tanah hingga sebatas lutut, dan ia pun terjatuh."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Shaken, Suraqah begged them for a promise of safety and offered them provisions. They asked only, “Keep our whereabouts hidden.” ‘Amir wrote the promise on leather, and Suraqah rode back, turning every pursuer home."
msgstr "Dengan gemetar, Suraqah memohon jaminan keselamatan dan menawarkan bekal kepada mereka. Mereka hanya meminta, “Rahasiakan keberadaan kami.” ‘Amir menuliskan janji itu pada selembar kulit, lalu Suraqah berkuda kembali dan menyuruh setiap pengejar pulang."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah gave up the chase. They asked him to tell no one where they were, and he sent other searchers the wrong way."
msgstr "Suraqah menghentikan pengejarannya. Mereka memintanya agar tidak memberi tahu siapa pun tentang keberadaan mereka, dan ia mengarahkan para pencari lain ke jalan yang salah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hungry and far from home, they stopped at the tent of a woman called Umm Ma‘bad. She had no food to give them."
msgstr "Dalam keadaan lapar dan jauh dari rumah, mereka berhenti di tenda seorang perempuan bernama Umm Ma‘bad. Ia tidak punya makanan untuk diberikan kepada mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Her thin sheep had no milk. The Prophet ﷺ said Allah’s name and milked the sheep, and everyone drank!"
msgstr "Dombanya yang kurus tidak menghasilkan susu. Nabi ﷺ menyebut nama Allah lalu memerahnya, dan semua orang pun minum!"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After they left, her husband came home. She told him of their guest: a shining face, and words like beads on a string."
msgstr "Setelah mereka pergi, suaminya pulang. Ia bercerita tentang tamu mereka: wajah yang bercahaya dan kata-kata yang tersusun indah seperti manik-manik pada seutas tali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each morning the Ansar, the Muslims of Madinah, watched for him until the heat drove them in. Then a man on a fort saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Setiap pagi, kaum Ansar, kaum Muslim Madinah, menanti kedatangannya sampai terik matahari membuat mereka masuk kembali. Suatu hari, seorang lelaki di atas benteng melihat para musafir berpakaian putih berkilauan dalam fatamorgana. “Itulah orang yang kalian tunggu-tunggu!” serunya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him at Quba, a village just outside Madinah, resting under a palm with Abu Bakr. Most had never seen him, and greeted Abu Bakr, until the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr shaded him with his cloak."
msgstr "Mereka menemukannya di Quba, sebuah desa tepat di luar Madinah, sedang beristirahat di bawah pohon kurma bersama Abu Bakr. Kebanyakan dari mereka belum pernah melihatnya dan menyapa Abu Bakr, sampai sinar matahari mengenai Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakr menaunginya dengan jubahnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Ali caught up with him there. He had stayed three days in Makkah to return what people had left in the Prophet’s ﷺ care. At Quba the Prophet ﷺ founded his mosque, and on a Friday he rode on towards Madinah."
msgstr "‘Ali menyusulnya di sana. Ia tinggal selama tiga hari di Makkah untuk mengembalikan barang-barang yang dititipkan orang kepada Nabi ﷺ. Di Quba, Nabi ﷺ mendirikan masjidnya, lalu pada hari Jumat ia berkendara menuju Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last the Prophet ﷺ rode into Madinah on his camel. Everyone asked him to stay, but he let the camel choose the way."
msgstr "Akhirnya, Nabi ﷺ memasuki Madinah dengan menunggang unta. Semua orang memintanya untuk tinggal bersama mereka, tetapi beliau membiarkan unta itu memilih jalan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People climbed up high to see him. His camel knelt in a yard where dates were dried, and there he made his home."
msgstr "Orang-orang naik ke tempat yang tinggi agar dapat melihatnya. Untanya berlutut di sebuah halaman tempat kurma dijemur, dan di sanalah beliau menetap."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He prayed that Allah would make the Muslims love Madinah as much as Makkah, and even more."
msgstr "Beliau berdoa agar Allah menjadikan kaum Muslim mencintai Madinah seperti mereka mencintai Makkah, bahkan lebih."

