#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the guide came with the camels, as arranged, and ‘Amir left his flock to go with them. The four set out: the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr with ‘Amir behind him, and the guide, down along the coast, “by the edge of the sea.”"
msgstr "Kemudian pemandu datang membawa unta-unta, sesuai kesepakatan, dan ‘Amir meninggalkan ternaknya untuk ikut bersama mereka. Mereka berempat pun berangkat: Nabi ﷺ, Abu Bakr dengan ‘Amir di belakangnya, dan sang pemandu, menyusuri pesisir, “di tepi laut.”"

#: src/lib/scene-manifest.js
msgid "N09d"
msgstr "N09d"

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "Next stage"
msgstr "Tahap berikutnya"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Closer and closer he came, until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ never looked back; Abu Bakr kept turning round. As Suraqah drew near, the ground gave way: his horse sank to its knees, and he fell."
msgstr "Ia semakin mendekat, hingga bisa mendengar Nabi ﷺ membaca. Nabi ﷺ tidak pernah menoleh ke belakang; Abu Bakr terus menoleh. Saat Suraqah semakin dekat, tanah amblas: kudanya terperosok hingga lutut, dan ia terjatuh."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the cry the Muslims hurried out to meet him, and he went with them to Quba, just outside Madinah. Most had never seen him and greeted Abu Bakr, until the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr shaded him with his cloak."
msgstr "Mendengar seruan itu, kaum Muslim bergegas menyambutnya. Ia pun pergi bersama mereka ke Quba, di luar Madinah. Kebanyakan dari mereka belum pernah melihatnya dan menyangka Abu Bakr-lah yang mereka sambut, sampai matahari menyinari Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakr menaungi beliau dengan jubahnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Word had reached Madinah that the Prophet ﷺ had left Makkah. Every morning after the dawn prayer, its Muslims, the Ansar, walked out to the edge of the lava plain and watched for him, until the sun took the last of the shade and drove them home."
msgstr "Kabar bahwa Nabi ﷺ telah meninggalkan Makkah sampai di Madinah. Setiap pagi setelah salat Subuh, kaum Muslim di sana, kaum Ansar, berjalan ke tepi dataran lava dan menanti beliau sampai matahari menghilangkan tempat berteduh yang tersisa dan membuat mereka pulang."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Madinah, people went out every morning to wait for him, until the sun grew too hot."
msgstr "Di Madinah, orang-orang keluar setiap pagi untuk menantikan beliau, sampai matahari terasa terlalu terik."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One day, when they had already given up and gone in, the first to see him was not one of them at all. A Jewish man on one of the forts saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Suatu hari, setelah mereka menyerah menunggu dan masuk kembali, orang pertama yang melihat beliau justru bukan salah seorang dari mereka. Seorang pria Yahudi di salah satu benteng melihat para musafir berpakaian putih berkilauan di tengah fatamorgana. “Itu dia, orang yang kalian tunggu-tunggu!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One day, a man up on a tower saw travellers in white coming. “He is here!” he shouted."
msgstr "Suatu hari, seorang pria di atas menara melihat para musafir berpakaian putih datang. “Beliau sudah tiba!” serunya."

#: src/lib/scene-manifest.js
msgid "N05c"
msgstr "N05c"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Those first months were hard: Madinah was then a land of fever. Abu Bakr and Bilal fell ill, and Bilal longed aloud for the valleys of Makkah. So the Prophet ﷺ prayed: “O Allah, make Madinah dear to us as You made Makkah dear to us, or dearer.”"
msgstr "Bulan-bulan pertama itu terasa berat: saat itu Madinah adalah negeri yang dilanda demam. Abu Bakr dan Bilal jatuh sakit, dan Bilal mengungkapkan kerinduannya pada lembah-lembah Makkah. Maka, Nabi ﷺ berdoa, “Ya Allah, jadikanlah Madinah kami cintai sebagaimana kami mencintai Makkah, atau bahkan lebih.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr offered him one of the two camels he had kept ready. “At its price,” the Prophet ﷺ said. They handed both to a guide they had hired, to bring to Mount Thawr after three nights."
msgstr "Abu Bakr menawarkan salah satu dari dua unta yang telah ia siapkan kepadanya. “Dengan membayarnya,” kata Nabi ﷺ. Mereka menyerahkan kedua unta itu kepada seorang penunjuk jalan yang telah mereka sewa, untuk dibawa ke Gunung Thawr setelah tiga malam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr gave a guide their two camels, to bring to a mountain called Thawr after three nights."
msgstr "Abu Bakr menyerahkan dua unta mereka kepada seorang penunjuk jalan, untuk dibawa ke sebuah gunung bernama Thawr setelah tiga malam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then food was made ready for the road. There was nothing to tie the bag with, so Asma, Abu Bakr’s daughter, split her waistband in two, and from then on she was called “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Lalu makanan disiapkan untuk bekal di perjalanan. Tidak ada tali untuk mengikat kantong itu, jadi Asma, putri Abu Bakr, membelah ikat pinggangnya menjadi dua. Sejak saat itu, ia dikenal sebagai “perempuan pemilik dua ikat pinggang”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Abu Bakr’s house, Asma made their food for the road. Finding nothing to tie the bag and the water skin with, she told her father, “Only my waistband.” “Split it in two,” he said, and so she was called “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Di rumah Abu Bakr, Asma menyiapkan bekal untuk perjalanan mereka. Karena tak menemukan apa pun untuk mengikat kantong dan kantong air, ia berkata kepada ayahnya, “Hanya ikat pinggangku.” “Belah menjadi dua,” kata ayahnya. Sejak itu, ia dikenal sebagai “perempuan dengan dua ikat pinggang”."
